    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d771">

                <pb facs="0825" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.20/293: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Colombia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-19T18:30:00-04:00">June 19, 1944—6:30
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–434. Your 706 of April 14.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d771-f1"/> The Department has
                    received a letter from the Secretary of War<anchor n="21" xml:id="d771-f2"/>
                    with reference to training of Colombian Army Aviators for combat duty stating
                    that views transmitted in War Department’s letter of May 22 (see Department’s
                    A–417 of June 13<anchor n="22" xml:id="d771-f3"/>) are also applicable to the
                    employment of small groups of aviators from any of the American Republics. War
                    Department adds however that in appreciation of the beneficial effect which such
                    cooperation would have on our relations with these countries, it is now
                    investigating the feasibility of establishing a special training program whereby
                    courses of instruction in appropriate phases of military activity would be
                    offered to the military personnel from such countries.</p>
                <p>War Department has informally stated that such a program, even if found to be
                    feasible, would not make it possible to utilize the trained men in active
                    theaters.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d771-f1" n="20" xml:id="d771-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d771-f2" n="21" xml:id="d771-f2-content">
                <p>Henry L. Stimson.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d771-f3" n="22" xml:id="d771-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed; it quoted the War Department’s letter of May 22, 1944, which
                    indicated that the disadvantages of arranging for 300 Colombians to serve
                    actively in the war outweighed the advantages (821.20/293).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
